{
	chapter.1000000000000001.chapter_subtitle: ["Food, water, climate, stone tools, straw, pottery, and the first steps toward copper."]
	chapter.1000000000000001.title: "Stone Age"
	chapter.1000000000000002.chapter_subtitle: ["The first stable metal, casting, a copper anvil, and early preparation for mechanical power."]
	chapter.1000000000000002.title: "Copper/Bronze Age"
	chapter.1000000000000004.chapter_subtitle: ["Cast iron, bloom, wrought iron, and the first serious casings."]
	chapter.1000000000000004.title: "Iron Age"
	chapter.1000000000000006.chapter_subtitle: ["Rubber, resin, pumps, engines, and heavy mechanization before full electricity."]
	chapter.1000000000000006.title: "Industrial Age"
	chapter.1000000000000007.chapter_subtitle: ["Early electricity, cables, hulls, circuits, and basic machines."]
	chapter.1000000000000007.title: "LV Electrical Age"
	chapter.1000000000000008.chapter_subtitle: ["MV/HV, oil, chemistry, stainless steel, aluminium, titanium, and advanced electronics."]
	chapter.1000000000000008.title: "Advanced Industry"
	chapter.72BB266DC9850667.title: "Millitary"
	quest.01AAA0C672C79A66.quest_desc: ["Early water wheels provide low-tech rotational power before engines dominate. They are useful where a river or channel can support them."]
	quest.01AAA0C672C79A66.title: "Water Wheel"
	quest.02DE0D80435AAAAA.quest_desc: ["Steel swords are the first serious steel blades. Higher steel variants improve durability and combat performance as forging progresses."]
	quest.034C79C5A64A4703.quest_desc: ["Leather armor is simple protection made from worked hides. It is useful before metal armor becomes practical."]
	quest.034C79C5A64A4703.title: "Leather Armor"
	quest.04ADDDEBAEC0FEC4.quest_desc: ["A hot air burner heats the air inside a balloon to help lift your craft. Provide fuel and size the balloon to suit the weight of the build."]
	quest.04DC559BCF7D3BF9.quest_desc: ["Early ore processing starts with manual crushing and washing. Powered washing can give byproducts later, but hand washing is intentionally simpler."]
	quest.04DC559BCF7D3BF9.title: "Ore Processing"
	quest.053253FDD26A991E.quest_desc: ["The turbine sits after the combustion chamber in a standard More Propulsion turbofan engine and uses energy from the hot gas flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.05651052965E463B.quest_desc: ["Thermometers make heat and climate easier to read directly. The later version builds on the simpler temperature instrument instead of replacing its role for free."]
	quest.062D8346AAD26F1A.quest_desc: ["Potatoes serve as ammunition for the potato cannon as well as food. The napalm variant adds an incendiary effect; test it away from your base."]
	quest.068E4A64B6441A50.quest_desc: ["The vector thruster uses FE power and allows directional thrust control. Supply energy and configure redstone controls to maneuver your craft."]
	quest.07232440F45E4B70.quest_desc: [
		"Primitive insulation and raw clothing are the first layer of climate protection. They are not a full seasonal outfit, but they can keep early weather from becoming a constant emergency."
		"Insulation is added on a Sewing Table. Blue or cyan insulation protects against cold, orange or red protects against heat, purple or neutral covers both sides less efficiently, and green or adaptive insulation shifts toward the current problem."
	]
	quest.079180C843C8A329.quest_desc: ["The chisel and sledgehammer expand copper-tier tool work. They are utility tools for shaping blocks and heavier manual work."]
	quest.07D3D536F74CC090.quest_desc: ["The solid fuel thruster accepts fuel from the rear. Arrange an item supply and use a redstone signal to switch thrust on and off."]
	quest.0847DBC1DEFEC89F.quest_desc: ["Bronze can come from several supported bronze alloys. Shared material tags let those variants share progression where the exact alloy is not the point."]
	quest.0847DBC1DEFEC89F.title: "Bronze Ingot"
	quest.08DACF0EB5CBB14A.quest_desc: ["Bellows improve heat control and are needed for several heat systems. They also mark the point where leather processing starts paying off."]
	quest.08F3AE24F79F88B1.quest_desc: ["Beds are a comfort and spawn tool, but they require proper textile progress rather than a quick vanilla wool recipe."]
	quest.08F3AE24F79F88B1.title: "Bed"
	quest.090F143FA904A97F.quest_desc: ["Stamens are an intermediate used for nails, rivets, and other small metal parts. Turning recipes help automate them later."]
	quest.090F3EF30426D4FA.quest_desc: ["The compressor prepares incoming air before the combustion chamber in a monstrous More Propulsion turbojet engine. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.09D35B334652CBC0.quest_desc: ["Tier 3 guncotton firearms use stronger propellant and more precise steel construction, but still avoid the highest late-game alloys."]
	quest.09D35B334652CBC0.title: "Tier 3 Guncotton Guns"
	quest.0A4617B66E27552B.quest_desc: ["The bloomery produces raw blooms that must still be worked into refined blooms before wrought iron becomes useful."]
	quest.0AD0DECE0BE3CD0B.quest_desc: ["The cutting board and juicer open more practical food preparation. They turn raw ingredients into meals and useful intermediate foods."]
	quest.0B1C18787FA20C6D.quest_desc: ["Melt early copper-bearing materials in a vessel and pour them into an ingot mold. This is the handoff from stone survival into metalworking."]
	quest.0BB552AE27BF12DC.quest_desc: ["The crucible is the serious alloying step. It works with the unified molten metals used by the rest of the material system."]
	quest.0BB552AE27BF12DC.title: "Crucible"
	quest.0BB6B852D162EABF.quest_desc: ["The bloomery is the bronze-age gate into iron. It turns iron ore into blooms, not clean pure iron."]
	quest.0BFC8E82B5D3CF3F.quest_desc: ["The helve hammer automates heavy hammer work. Bloom processing and similar heated hammering operations belong here, not in generic heated pressing."]
	quest.0C816AE96DA31980.quest_desc: ["Coke fuels the next stage of metallurgy. In this pack, the blast furnace requires coke; it can also fuel a charcoal forge."]
	quest.0CF7FFECE746826E.quest_desc: ["Steel javelins are the high-end form of the simple throwing weapon line. Red and blue steel versions are expensive but durable."]
	quest.0D5CD84C5AA9AC35.quest_desc: ["Build a pit kiln with straw and logs to fire unfired clay items. This is still your main ceramic route before dedicated kilns and machines."]
	quest.0D5CD84C5AA9AC35.title: "Pit Kiln"
	quest.0D6EC3FB0FF0657C.quest_desc: ["Wattle and daub are early building materials. They give a practical way to build before stone and metal construction take over."]
	quest.0E315AE89CC0E531.quest_desc: ["Flint tools are alternate early blades and ignition parts. Shape the flint chain by holding flint or flint scraps and right-clicking solid stone, not by using a normal crafting grid."]
	quest.0EE1DD2A4489F103.quest_desc: ["The nozzle forms the exhaust end of a large More Propulsion turbofan engine and directs the outgoing flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.0FF4263C6B13AC3E.quest_desc: ["The regular engine is a stronger mechanical option after the simplest portable and Stirling stages. Expect its recipe to lean on real engine parts."]
	quest.1100000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"Your first progression steps are survival, not a furnace rush. The vanilla furnace and vanilla metallurgy are not the intended early path."
		"Find food, water, stones, sticks, plant fiber, flint, and bones. Clay and a pit kiln come next."
	]
	quest.1100000000000001.title: "First Day"
	quest.1100000000000002.quest_desc: [
		"Collect loose rocks from the ground. This is the real start of the stone tool chain."
		"There are two stone-working routes. Classic knapping opens a pattern GUI and lets you shape tool heads directly. The alternate route is a world interaction: hold a loose rock or stone head and right-click a solid stone block."
		"The split chain is different from normal knapping: loose rock -> hammer head + shovel head; hammer head -> axe head; shovel head -> hoe head; hoe head -> knife head + javelin head; knife head -> javelin heads. Do not put these in a crafting grid; use right-click on stone. Outputs are chance-based, so bring extra stone."
	]
	quest.1100000000000002.title: "Loose Rock"
	quest.1100000000000004.quest_desc: ["The axe turns trees into a reliable material source. Felled trees become physical logs, so plan where they will fall."]
	quest.1100000000000004.title: "Stone Tools"
	quest.1100000000000005.quest_desc: ["The firestarter is the first controlled ignition source. Keep spares; early fire is intentionally unreliable."]
	quest.1100000000000005.title: "Firestarter"
	quest.1100000000000006.quest_desc: ["The firepit opens basic cooking and heating, but it is still not a vanilla furnace replacement."]
	quest.1100000000000006.title: "Firepit"
	quest.1100000000000007.quest_desc: ["Clay is the gate into pottery. Look for clay-bearing soil and surface markers near wet areas."]
	quest.1100000000000007.title: "Clay"
	quest.1100000000000008.quest_desc: ["The small vessel is your first important container for processing and carrying materials."]
	quest.1100000000000008.title: "Ceramic Vessel"
	quest.1100000000000009.quest_desc: ["Ingot molds prepare the transition into copper. Metal will still require charcoal and the right ore."]
	quest.1100000000000009.title: "Ingot Mold"
	quest.110000000000000B.quest_desc: ["Charcoal is the first serious fuel and the bridge into metalworking."]
	quest.110000000000000B.title: "Charcoal"
	quest.110000000000000C.quest_desc: ["Small native copper, malachite, or tetrahedrite on the surface tells you where the Copper Age begins."]
	quest.110000000000000C.title: "Copper Traces"
	quest.110000000000000D.quest_desc: ["Straw is needed for early structures, pottery, thatch, bedding, and several simple materials."]
	quest.110000000000000D.title: "Straw"
	quest.110000000000000F.quest_desc: ["Cut real trees carefully and expect logs to behave like physical objects."]
	quest.110000000000000F.title: "Felling Trees"
	quest.1100000000000010.quest_desc: ["Hunger and thirst are constant survival pressure. Eat varied meals and drink clean water instead of relying on one filler forever. Food nutrients raise your maximum health: a balanced diet with several nutrient groups makes you much tougher, while poor nutrition keeps your health low even if your hunger bar is full. Food also spoils over time, so preserve what you can, cook when needed, and build real winter stores before crops stop carrying you. Sawdust and other fillers can stretch meals in an emergency, but they are not a winter plan."]
	quest.1100000000000010.title: "Hunger and Thirst"
	quest.1100000000000012.quest_desc: ["The large vessel is the first large ceramic container. It supports storage and several low-tech processing steps before metal tanks."]
	quest.1100000000000012.title: "Large Vessel"
	quest.1100000000000017.quest_desc: [
		"Gather plant fiber from grass and twist it into plant string. Many stone tools need a binding material, not only a rock and a stick."
		"Plant string is also an early material bridge into straw work, simple tools, and later low-tech crafting."
	]
	quest.1100000000000017.title: "Plant Fiber"
	quest.1100000000000018.quest_desc: ["Pick up loose sticks from the ground with right-click, or break twigs. This branch leads into fire rather than stone tool shaping."]
	quest.1100000000000018.title: "Sticks"
	quest.1100000000000019.quest_desc: ["Flint is a useful early sharp material and a fallback for several survival recipes. To split flint, hold it and right-click a solid stone block; flint scraps and arrow heads use the same stone-clicking chain."]
	quest.1100000000000019.title: "Flint"
	quest.110000000000001A.quest_desc: ["Bones are an early material source from groundcover and animals. Hold a bone or bone scrap and right-click a solid stone block to split it into primitive tool parts. Bones also matter for glue, meal, and later utility recipes."]
	quest.110000000000001A.title: "Bone"
	quest.111922867CC7F722.quest_desc: ["Compressed coke clay and coke oven bricks start the low-tech coke oven line. This route is intentionally available before iron-heavy machinery."]
	quest.1200000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"Copper follows the cast-metal progression instead of the vanilla ingot route."
		"If a recipe asks for copper, use the copper ingot made through the normal casting chain."
	]
	quest.1200000000000001.title: "Copper Ingot"
	quest.1200000000000002.quest_desc: ["The anvil unlocks proper forging. Direct hammer crafting for plates is intentionally disabled."]
	quest.1200000000000002.title: "Copper Anvil"
	quest.1261AC20AECB6917.quest_desc: ["The mechanical press handles plate work, molding, and compression recipes that should not be simple hand crafts."]
	quest.12C7CC406C871B74.quest_desc: ["A steel anvil moves forging beyond wrought iron and prepares the higher steel tiers."]
	quest.131A405EC26E81C1.quest_desc: ["Use the blast furnace for steel-era metallurgy. Simpler primitive furnace progression is not the intended route here."]
	quest.13C9A5D51E7FB5A9.quest_desc: [
		"Quench-hardening is separate from forge quality. Steel tool heads can receive a quench result in addition to any forging bonus they already have."
		"Heat the tool head, then place the hot head into a barrel containing the quenching liquid."
		"Fresh water is the safest basic quench: it usually gives an expert result, with a smaller chance of perfect hardening and a smaller chance of a failed quench."
		"Oil water is steadier than fresh water, with a slightly better chance of perfect hardening and a lower failure risk."
		"Oil is the most reliable controlled quench: it can still produce perfect hardening, usually gives an expert result, and does not cause failed quench debuffs."
		"Salt water is the most aggressive quench: it has the highest chance of perfect hardening, but also the highest chance of a failed quench."
	]
	quest.13C9A5D51E7FB5A9.title: "Quench-Hardening"
	quest.1400000000000001.quest_desc: ["Iron ores smelt into cast iron. Pure iron is not a mass early product from ore."]
	quest.1400000000000001.title: "Cast Iron"
	quest.1400000000000003.quest_desc: ["Wrought iron is the canonical replacement for early iron in most recipes. It cannot be obtained by simple remelting."]
	quest.1400000000000003.title: "Wrought Iron"
	quest.1408EB67CA96DC67.quest_desc: ["The combustion chamber burns fuel in a monstrous More Propulsion turbofan engine. In this pack, GTCEu light fuel fills the kerosene role for these engines. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.14C11CAF8C6E87C3.quest_desc: ["The combustion chamber burns fuel in a standard More Propulsion turbojet engine. In this pack, GTCEu light fuel fills the kerosene role for these engines. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.14EA33EC86BE9029.quest_desc: ["Backpacks are storage upgrades, not mobile factories. Only a small set of QoL backpack upgrades is intended to remain available."]
	quest.152DDD9C3BA36B82.quest_desc: [
		"Linen clothing is a breathable plant-fiber outfit, stronger and more comfortable than crude early clothing but still lighter than wool or fur. It is a good everyday set for mild and warm climates."
		"{\"text\":\"Orange\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"/\",\"color\":\"white\"},{\"text\":\"Red\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" insulation fits linen best when you want a light outfit for warm travel.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.152DDD9C3BA36B82.title: "Linen Clothes"
	quest.15846E97B55E4C03.quest_desc: ["Early baskets and crates matter because inventory pressure is part of survival. Use them before metal logistics takes over."]
	quest.1600000000000003.quest_desc: ["The portable engine is a mid-stage power source. It should be easier than diesel, but not free."]
	quest.1600000000000003.title: "Portable Engine"
	quest.1600000000000004.quest_desc: ["The diesel engine is a more advanced and expensive form of mechanical power tied to steel components and the fuel chain."]
	quest.1600000000000004.title: "Diesel Engine"
	quest.160B48C0DBF93BBD.quest_desc: [
		"Primitive clothing is rough emergency gear for the first seasons. It is best used as a temporary buffer against mild cold or heat until proper cloth outfits are available."
		"{\"text\":\"Purple/Neutral\",\"color\":\"light_purple\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation is the most sensible use here: primitive clothing is a stopgap, not a specialized winter or desert set.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.160B48C0DBF93BBD.title: "Primitive Clothes"
	quest.16B25A93BEC5CACE.quest_desc: ["Treated wood is made with creosote. Barrel soaking is the intended route; bucket crafts are removed."]
	quest.16E0B307489B86A3.quest_desc: ["Gather sticks into bunches and bundles to keep a compact supply. These are useful in recipes that need more wood than a single stick."]
	quest.1700000000000001.quest_desc: ["The LV machine hull is the main gate into the true electrical age."]
	quest.1700000000000001.title: "LV Machine Hull"
	quest.1700000000000002.quest_desc: ["Circuit progression remains the main limit of the electrical era. Mechanical components should support this stage, not bypass it."]
	quest.1700000000000002.title: "Basic Circuit"
	quest.1700000000000003.quest_desc: ["The mechanical lathe can handle many early turning jobs, while this electrical lathe becomes the more reliable machine standard."]
	quest.1700000000000003.title: "LV Lathe"
	quest.1700000000000004.quest_desc: ["Electrical ore processing gives deeper processing, but byproducts are adjusted toward more realistic materials."]
	quest.1700000000000004.title: "LV Macerator"
	quest.171E066BBA9C9590.quest_desc: ["Pre-steel swords are bronze-age weapons. They are useful before steel, but they should not replace proper steel blades forever."]
	quest.171E066BBA9C9590.title: "Pre-Steel Swords"
	quest.17D786CD9696C663.quest_desc: ["The sledgehammer is the heavier companion to normal hammers. Use it for jobs that need force rather than fine shaping."]
	quest.17D918A2CBDE9961.quest_desc: ["Proper workbenches replace the vanilla crafting table in many recipes. Build one once you can make proper lumber."]
	quest.17D918A2CBDE9961.title: "Workbench"
	quest.1800000000000001.quest_desc: ["Stainless steel and chromium are unified around a single material chain to avoid duplicate ingots, plates, and fluids."]
	quest.1800000000000001.title: "Stainless Steel"
	quest.1800000000000002.quest_desc: ["Aluminium becomes an important structural material for aviation, engines, and later mechanisms."]
	quest.1800000000000002.title: "Aluminium"
	quest.1800000000000003.quest_desc: ["Synthetic rubber follows the oil chemistry chain from the proper intermediate components. Shortcuts that skip those stages are disabled."]
	quest.1800000000000003.title: "Synthetic Rubber"
	quest.1800000000000004.quest_desc: ["Magnetic materials are unified around dedicated magnetic ingots, plates, and blocks instead of a separate duplicate alloy."]
	quest.1800000000000004.title: "Magnetic Materials"
	quest.183DBBCEDEB4544A.quest_desc: ["The trip hammer and steel pump mark heavier mechanical infrastructure. They belong after steel work is established."]
	quest.189FA5CEAE8867F4.quest_desc: ["The encased fan is useful mechanical infrastructure. When powered and placed correctly, it can replace bellows for heat systems that need airflow."]
	quest.18C87A8331734DCE.quest_desc: ["Potato cannons are simple ranged utility weapons. Mounted versions belong with heavier mechanical assemblies."]
	quest.18EE80F7F03F5CF4.quest_desc: ["Reinforced fire bricks advance your heat-resistant materials. In this pack, they are used to craft the Create Metallurgy industrial crucible."]
	quest.19145F5A6C371929.quest_desc: ["Gunpowder charge size matters. Tiny piles, small piles, normal powder, and packed charges represent different cartridge loads."]
	quest.192E98B7D45B0AE7.quest_desc: [
		"Cotton clothing is light, breathable gear for warm seasons and hot regions. It is not a winter set, but it is comfortable when overheating is the bigger danger."
		"{\"text\":\"Purple/Neutral\",\"color\":\"light_purple\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation is cotton's main role: broad light protection for mixed everyday weather.\",\"color\":\"white\"},{\"text\":\" Blue/Cyan\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},{\"text\":\" adds a small cold-side bias, so it can help a little when temperatures dip without becoming a winter outfit.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.192E98B7D45B0AE7.title: "Cotton Clothes"
	quest.194C8BD503B7824A.quest_desc: ["Wind power is an early renewable mechanical source, but it still needs cloth and proper mechanical setup."]
	quest.1984143A17F54ED5.quest_desc: ["Windmill blades come from loom-made cloth. This keeps large early power sources tied to agriculture and textile work."]
	quest.1984143A17F54ED5.title: "Windmill"
	quest.198DBCA8CD28476E.quest_desc: ["The prospector's pick is the correct tool for locating deeper ore bodies after surface traces run out."]
	quest.1A646F5E6A26E0CE.quest_desc: ["Wooden multiblock tanks give early bulk fluid storage before metal tanks and electric pumps become comfortable."]
	quest.1A646F5E6A26E0CE.title: "Wooden Multiblock Tank"
	quest.1AA0060656FD9BA8.quest_desc: ["A charcoal pit is the scalable charcoal route. The quest asks for a larger batch because metalworking consumes fuel quickly."]
	quest.1AA0060656FD9BA8.title: "Charcoal Pit"
	quest.1B31811F67A97289.quest_desc: ["Tier 2 gunpowder firearms add better materials and more complete mechanisms while still using conventional black powder loads."]
	quest.1B31811F67A97289.title: "Tier 2 Gunpowder Guns"
	quest.1BB15EFEA542C45F.quest_desc: ["The nozzle forms the exhaust end of a large More Propulsion turbojet engine and directs the outgoing flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.1DC1487FAD35E112.quest_desc: ["The brick coke oven turns coal into coke for hotter metallurgy. Lignite gives the lowest yield, bituminous coal is better, and anthracite gives the most coke per piece."]
	quest.1DC1487FAD35E112.title: "Coke Oven"
	quest.1DEAFF215DB3124B.quest_desc: ["Tier 1 guncotton firearms introduce cleaner, stronger propellant for weapons that still rely mostly on steel construction."]
	quest.1DEAFF215DB3124B.title: "Tier 1 Guncotton Guns"
	quest.1E13C86414920C57.quest_desc: ["Firmalife beekeeping supports food and material chains. It is optional, but useful once woodworking is stable."]
	quest.1E911D6BC074BC6F.quest_desc: ["A bronze anvil is the real start of bronze-tier forging and prepares the transition toward bloomery iron."]
	quest.1E911D6BC074BC6F.title: "Bronze Anvil"
	quest.1EC4E3B26941EDDD.quest_desc: ["Radial engines are a more complex engine path. They belong after simpler mechanical engines, not at the start of power generation."]
	quest.1F487C93822B190B.quest_desc: ["A wrought iron anvil is the baseline anvil for serious iron-age work and many later forging recipes."]
	quest.20A2781A8A2AD9E7.quest_desc: ["Red and blue steel buckets handle fluids that ordinary containers cannot. They are late metal tools, not early shortcuts."]
	quest.20A2781A8A2AD9E7.title: "Red and Blue Steel Buckets"
	quest.21A442A498A8F08F.quest_desc: ["The liquid vector thruster combines fuel-powered thrust with directional control. Supply fuel from below and set up redstone signals to control the engine."]
	quest.23F28A68974F8634.quest_desc: ["The turbine sits after the combustion chamber in a monstrous More Propulsion turbofan engine and uses energy from the hot gas flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.254458BB76CE6394.quest_desc: ["The crankshaft is a precision mechanical part for more serious engines and moving assemblies."]
	quest.258FB389085D5C46.quest_desc: ["Metal buckets and cans are compact fluid and food containers. Their recipes are tied to proper metalworking rather than simple vanilla crafts."]
	quest.259F5DA36110C1BD.quest_desc: ["Black steel is a major steel tier. It requires more alloy work and leads into the red and blue steel end of the traditional forging line."]
	quest.25A01E629A546DE8.quest_desc: ["The TFMG pipe bomb is an explosive weapon for combat and block destruction. Use it away from allies, stored supplies, and important structures."]
	quest.261EF74F869ADD67.quest_desc: ["The quern turns grain into flour. Food processing is part of progression because long expeditions and mining need reliable meals."]
	quest.261EF74F869ADD67.title: "Flour"
	quest.266D3339B7444D3B.quest_desc: ["The compressor prepares incoming air before the combustion chamber in a small More Propulsion turbofan engine. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.267410AB04A71900.quest_desc: ["Mittens are early heat protection. They make handling hot items less punishing, but metal tongs are still better later."]
	quest.2743BC35CA14BA64.quest_desc: ["The nozzle forms the exhaust end of a small More Propulsion turbojet engine and directs the outgoing flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.27CC5C4B1CE0745A.quest_desc: ["The nozzle forms the exhaust end of a standard More Propulsion turbofan engine and directs the outgoing flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.287D83696E62DC6C.quest_desc: ["The mechanical pump is the first practical fluid mover and becomes important for engines, soaking, and processing chains."]
	quest.289860FC89B80983.quest_desc: ["Horsepower is a low-tech mechanical option before engines. It fits the pre-electric part of the pack without bypassing metallurgy."]
	quest.28F265334755D336.quest_desc: ["Sandwiches are compact, practical food for travel and mining. They reward building up grain, vegetable, meat, and dairy infrastructure."]
	quest.28F265334755D336.title: "Sandwiches"
	quest.292D9BFE92914C72.quest_desc: ["Crates and wooden chests are early organized storage. Compatible crate variants share recipes through a common tag."]
	quest.292D9BFE92914C72.title: "Crates"
	quest.2A25D9AC41DA4DD0.quest_desc: ["The belt grinder automates polishing and grinding-style recipes where abrasion is more appropriate than cutting or hammering."]
	quest.2A677AC839BECEE9.quest_desc: ["Nitro powder and hardened nitro are stronger explosive materials. They should be treated as later chemical products, not early gunpowder substitutes."]
	quest.2A873B3AF6276B8D.quest_desc: ["Walking canes are optional utility items. They sit naturally in the wood-and-cloth stage of progression."]
	quest.2A9BBB0B1E6EB45A.quest_desc: ["Fishing gives a reliable food option once you can forge a hook. It is not required for metal progression, but helps survival."]
	quest.2A9BBB0B1E6EB45A.title: "Fishing"
	quest.2AF48211F7D699A9.quest_desc: ["Flamethrowers and cannon-style tools move ranged equipment into powered or fuel-based weaponry."]
	quest.2BAFD4A89829DB8D.quest_desc: ["Advanced chemical sprayers and heavy potato cannons are specialist weapons. They require more infrastructure than simple handheld ranged tools."]
	quest.2C05527A688B87E3.quest_desc: ["Bronze double ingots are the investment step for a bronze anvil. Any supported bronze alloy can satisfy this shared material tag."]
	quest.2C05527A688B87E3.title: "Bronze Double Ingot"
	quest.2C19D97121EC1110.quest_desc: ["Juicing and bowl processing support better food preparation. Use them to turn crops into more useful meals and ingredients."]
	quest.2CEFAB5A303E092F.quest_desc: ["An encased fan creates airflow for item processing. Plain air also speeds up cooling of TFC molds and Create Metallurgy casting tables: the effect scales with speed, reaching ×2 at 256 RPM."]
	quest.2D3ABA160CBE63B5.quest_desc: ["Kaolin clay and kaolinite powder are part of the refractory material chain. Kaolin is not ordinary clay and should be treated as a higher-value material."]
	quest.2D43505233CEBF41.quest_desc: ["The large engine is a late mechanical power source. Its cost should reflect the jump from simple engines to heavy machinery."]
	quest.2DA40A40B345D125.quest_desc: ["Shift + Right Click with Bowl in Hands to make Salad"]
	quest.2E6EF8C65D438E49.quest_desc: ["Glassworking starts with dedicated tools. Blowpipes, jacks, paddles, and gem saws are the foundation for shaped glass and later precision parts."]
	quest.2E6EF8C65D438E49.title: "Glassworking"
	quest.2EF8CE6B4888448A.quest_desc: ["Tier 2 guncotton firearms use better propellant and more developed mechanisms than the first guncotton weapons."]
	quest.2EF8CE6B4888448A.title: "Tier 2 Guncotton Guns"
	quest.2F00B00A0353550A.quest_desc: ["Water wheels are the native water-power path. They are separate from larger mechanical wheels and fit the low-tech mechanical stage."]
	quest.2F00B00A0353550A.title: "Water Wheel"
	quest.2F85B7F8E8379AE7.quest_desc: ["A ceramic spindle begins the thread and yarn chain before metal machines. Fire it like other pottery."]
	quest.30719285194168FE.quest_desc: [
		"Temperature follows the world around you: seasons, local climate, time of day, weather, elevation, nearby heat sources, and water all matter. Cold Sweat adds body temperature on top of that climate."
		"The colored insulation bars on clothing show how that item protects you:"
		"{\"text\":\"Blue/Cyan\",\"color\":\"aqua\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation protects from cold and freezing.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"Orange\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"/\",\"color\":\"white\"},{\"text\":\"Red\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" insulation protects from heat and overheating.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"Purple/Neutral\",\"color\":\"light_purple\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation covers both sides at once, but is less specialized than dedicated heat or cold protection.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"Green/Adaptive\",\"color\":\"green\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation shifts toward the condition you are currently facing.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
		"Use thermometers to read the situation, and use clothing plus insulation to prepare for winter, summer, mountains, deserts, and hot work near forges. Insulation is added with a Sewing Table."
	]
	quest.30719285194168FE.title: "Temperature"
	quest.3076CF717A400D8B.quest_desc: ["Chemical sprayers and turrets are specialist equipment. They fit after basic weapon and fuel handling is established."]
	quest.30BD561A7A6EA4B1.quest_desc: ["Food additives extend cooking options. Sawdust is treated as a low-value edible filler, while milling and quern work support flour chains."]
	quest.30BD561A7A6EA4B1.quest_subtitle: "We can add sawdust to meals to make them more filling, if not exactly tasty - or healthy"
	quest.30BD561A7A6EA4B1.title: "Food additives"
	quest.3184D76C3F4E234A.quest_desc: ["Flatbread is the first comfortable bread route. It turns grain processing into reliable travel food."]
	quest.3184D76C3F4E234A.title: "First Bread"
	quest.31997A3F35F2DC40.quest_desc: ["Obsidian and high-end primitive weapons are strong survival tools before full metal combat equipment."]
	quest.31AB8BE3E7997CBA.quest_desc: ["Red and blue steel anvils are the top anvil tier and mark the end of the traditional forging line."]
	quest.31B0D1EF75ECBD91.quest_desc: ["Empty cans allow long-term food storage. Canning becomes stronger once sterilization and cleaning are available."]
	quest.31FEED38425FCDB8.quest_desc: ["A steam vent fills the balloon above it with steam to generate lift. Supply the boiler with water and heat; a redstone signal controls steam output."]
	quest.3334D8C9EBACBC5C.quest_desc: ["The compressor prepares incoming air before the combustion chamber in a standard More Propulsion turbofan engine. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.335BA2499DAFB1A8.quest_desc: ["A powder keg clears large sections of rock with an explosion. Account for nearby structures and move to a safe distance before detonation."]
	quest.33E49B6E8A8CE524.quest_desc: ["Tier 1 gunpowder firearms are early steel guns with better mechanisms than the simplest models, but still use black powder ammunition."]
	quest.33E49B6E8A8CE524.title: "Tier 1 Gunpowder Guns"
	quest.355B5C36B6D05539.quest_desc: ["Rods are a major intermediate. They feed rivets, rings, wires, springs, handles, and machine recipes."]
	quest.380009CABCAD8273.quest_desc: ["A burner uses fuel to heat production equipment. Check which fuels it accepts and arrange a supply before starting the installation."]
	quest.3897FD62BD9205D7.quest_desc: ["Potholders are cloth-based heat protection. They are less industrial than tongs but useful before better tools are available."]
	quest.3897FD62BD9205D7.title: "Potholders"
	quest.3A0130A8D0BC10E9.quest_desc: ["The huge diesel engine is intentionally expensive and tied to blast-furnace infrastructure. It should feel like a major power upgrade."]
	quest.3AD8A6CAFEC100AE.quest_desc: ["Cutting fish yields fish bones as well as fillets. Grind the bones into bone meal to put the remains of your catch to use."]
	quest.3CA52C36A2CC605B.quest_desc: ["The sluice gives low-tech washing and gathering utility without replacing full ore processing chains."]
	quest.3CA52C36A2CC605B.title: "Sluice"
	quest.3CC1DF3CB576C5FE.quest_desc: ["Glue is made from bone meal and becomes a practical binder for wood, leather, and utility recipes."]
	quest.3DB084E7A3A6E944.quest_desc: ["Support beams can be made before metal saws. Strip a log first, then hold an axe and right-click the stripped log or wood to rough-cut supports. The axe route has low yield and tool wear; proper saws remain much more efficient."]
	quest.3DB084E7A3A6E944.title: "Support Beams"
	quest.3E2EFA41938D7EFD.quest_desc: ["Rose gold is an early alloy branch used by several decorative and progression recipes."]
	quest.3F32730F6D83ADBD.quest_desc: ["Bone meal is a simple processed bone product and leads into glue and agriculture support."]
	quest.3F7F614121E34E01.quest_desc: ["Steel pumps and crankshafts are practical machine parts for stronger mechanical systems."]
	quest.3F93605EDE7A876B.quest_desc: [
		"Silk clothing is refined, light travel gear for variable or warm climates. It is better than rough early clothing and stays useful when you want protection without heavy winter bulk."
		"{\"text\":\"Green/Adaptive\",\"color\":\"green\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation suits silk well for travel, because the outfit is light and useful when conditions change.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.3F93605EDE7A876B.title: "Silk Clothes"
	quest.40531D671C1D1818.quest_desc: ["The curving press and power loom automate specialized shaping and textile work. They are important for larger mechanical production chains."]
	quest.410ECB07011FD0AC.quest_desc: ["Barrels are essential processing blocks, not just storage. Use them for leather work, soaking recipes, and several material conversions."]
	quest.410ECB07011FD0AC.title: "Barrel"
	quest.4129C8BFFAC8E4B8.quest_desc: ["Wooden tongs let you handle hot items early. They are more durable than ordinary wooden tools, but still a temporary solution before metal tongs."]
	quest.41580C5BAECF0CAE.quest_desc: ["Stirling engines and their burners are early mechanical engines. They are balanced below portable engines and use iron-age materials rather than late steel."]
	quest.41A9B18EA289F755.quest_desc: ["The gyroscopic mechanism is made from a precision mechanism through sequenced assembly. It is used in advanced control systems, including the smart propeller."]
	quest.41B356618789C6D6.quest_desc: ["The combustion chamber burns fuel in a large More Propulsion turbofan engine. In this pack, GTCEu light fuel fills the kerosene role for these engines. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.4484F1E91728CD18.quest_desc: ["Copper hoes and scythes make early farming and plant collection more efficient. They are practical tools, not combat progression."]
	quest.44B892B4B8FD1AED.quest_desc: ["The compressor prepares incoming air before the combustion chamber in a small More Propulsion turbojet engine. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.44F30EFA34EB4B07.quest_desc: ["Tier 4 nitro firearms use advanced propellant and more demanding materials. They belong after the basic firearm chain is mature."]
	quest.44F30EFA34EB4B07.title: "Tier 4 Nitro Guns"
	quest.465CAAA0689771F0.quest_desc: ["The copper pickaxe is the first real mining tool. Use it to move from surface traces into proper ore deposits."]
	quest.46F5A8C7B27438D8.quest_desc: ["Beekeeper protection makes hive work safer. It is optional, but useful if wax, honey, or related materials become important."]
	quest.46F5A8C7B27438D8.title: "Beekeeper Protection"
	quest.477F56CEAFC34197.quest_desc: ["The ion thruster is a late-stage electric propulsion option requiring advanced electronics. Provide FE power and redstone control before putting it into service on a craft."]
	quest.478ABE068E3CC3E5.quest_desc: ["Tier 6 armor-piercing firearms use the strongest AP materials and late-game construction requirements."]
	quest.478ABE068E3CC3E5.title: "Tier 6 AP Guns"
	quest.47A23ABB2E9D1716.quest_desc: [
		"Plant clothes are the simplest fiber outfit. They are weak and temporary, but useful during the first days when even a small climate buffer matters."
		"{\"text\":\"Purple/Neutral\",\"color\":\"light_purple\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation is the practical choice for plant clothes: weak, cheap, and useful only as early mixed protection.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.47A23ABB2E9D1716.title: "Plant Clothes"
	quest.4844F41F64A6483E.quest_desc: ["Pumice is useful for working stone and crafting an icebox. Save the pieces you find for more than just building."]
	quest.48F3A0C8ABBFE899.quest_desc: ["The combustion chamber burns fuel in a small More Propulsion turbofan engine. In this pack, GTCEu light fuel fills the kerosene role for these engines. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.49EE02CCEC95D0F7.quest_desc: ["Mechanical water wheels can work with river water. Rivers provide the best output, but player-built channels remain useful instead of being hard-blocked."]
	quest.4A5BA00DF8FB292F.quest_desc: ["Rolling and curving machines automate sheet, pipe, and shaped metal work that should not be simple hand crafting."]
	quest.4AF1F127B7BC33C5.quest_desc: ["Unfired clay items are shaped first and fired later. Tool molds are required for early casting, while vessels and jugs carry the survival economy."]
	quest.4AF1F127B7BC33C5.title: "Unfired Clay Molds And Tools"
	quest.4B10FE58DAC0C662.quest_desc: ["Steel comes after bloomery iron and the blast furnace. It is not produced by skipping directly through simple basin mixing."]
	quest.4BC02698E4B8398D.quest_desc: ["Claim the movement guide from this quest reward to learn the moves provided by ParCool. Check your control settings for the assigned keys."]
	quest.4BC02698E4B8398D.title: "Movements"
	quest.4C97DE5E37B09382.quest_desc: [
		"Burlap clothing is cheap, rough, and breathable. It fits early temperate or warm travel better than deep winter, and it is a practical step between plant clothes and better textiles."
		"{\"text\":\"Purple/Neutral\",\"color\":\"light_purple\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation is burlap's real role: cheap mixed protection that helps a bit on both sides, but does not specialize in severe cold or heat.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.4C97DE5E37B09382.title: "Burlap Clothes"
	quest.4D85F7D97E5C075C.quest_desc: ["Gold is mostly a specialist metal for mechanisms, electronics, and currency rather than basic tools."]
	quest.4E2BF256575ED45E.quest_desc: ["The spring coiling machine automates springs, rings, wire coils, and similar coiled parts from rods and fine wire."]
	quest.4E92681429999E11.quest_desc: ["A metal grill expands your campfire cooking options. Place it over the fire and use it to grill food."]
	quest.4F2193B75F3BE965.quest_desc: ["Tier 4 gunpowder firearms are late black-powder weapons with stronger materials and more complete construction."]
	quest.4F2193B75F3BE965.title: "Tier 4 Gunpowder Guns"
	quest.4F9A67618F6706DE.quest_desc: ["Shovels and excavators cover digging work. The larger tool is better for bulk terrain work once metal toolmaking is ready."]
	quest.4FA644197DDBF508.quest_desc: ["This thruster runs on liquid fuel. Supply it through pipes and use a redstone signal to activate thrust."]
	quest.4FD6AC216ACF8E12.quest_desc: ["Tier 6 nitro firearms sit at the top of the conventional firearm line, using advanced propellants and high-tier materials."]
	quest.4FD6AC216ACF8E12.title: "Tier 6 Nitro Guns"
	quest.4FE9ED58B22A56D4.quest_desc: ["Copper double ingots are welded on an anvil with flux. This prepares the seven double ingots needed for the copper anvil."]
	quest.50F3F8311E3AF995.quest_desc: ["Brass is an important early alloy for mechanisms and fittings. It complements bronze rather than replacing it."]
	quest.513F3C5028DFD854.quest_desc: ["The nozzle forms the exhaust end of a monstrous More Propulsion turbofan engine and directs the outgoing flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.5160DCFF7CD2F1E4.quest_desc: [
		"Wool clothing is the dependable cold-weather textile set. Use it for winter, highlands, and cold biomes; in hot seasons it can become a liability if you keep stacking cold protection."
		"{\"text\":\"Blue/Cyan\",\"color\":\"aqua\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation is the natural match for wool: stack it when winter, altitude, or cold biomes are the problem.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.5160DCFF7CD2F1E4.title: "Wool Clothes"
	quest.523C6394AFC91646.quest_desc: ["Tier 3 gunpowder firearms are improved black-powder weapons with better steel construction and more complex internals."]
	quest.523C6394AFC91646.title: "Tier 3 Gunpowder Guns"
	quest.5267E5618C972EF1.quest_desc: ["Fire bricks are needed for equipment that operates at high temperatures. Prepare a supply for metallurgy and for making reinforced fire bricks later."]
	quest.5377AF696D339F05.quest_desc: ["The quern and handstone are the first crushing system. They handle grain and several early manual processing recipes before machines."]
	quest.541F330719897F8D.quest_desc: ["The large diesel engine is a stronger version of diesel power and should come after the basic engine chain."]
	quest.5599C5E8D8A51F36.quest_desc: ["Red and blue steel ingots are the final steel materials. They are expensive, but they unlock the strongest traditional anvils and tools."]
	quest.5599C5E8D8A51F36.title: "Red/Blue Steel Ingot"
	quest.560F2039395D2B93.quest_desc: ["A water thruster propels a vessel through water. Position it to produce thrust along the intended direction of travel and test it after launching."]
	quest.568E6D8833E72A49.quest_desc: ["The mechanical mixer handles basin mixing, including heat-gated recipes. Some alloy and metal shortcuts are deliberately removed from ordinary mixing."]
	quest.5698D507553313B1.quest_desc: ["Tier 3 nitro firearms use stronger chemical propellant while staying below the most advanced firearm materials."]
	quest.5698D507553313B1.title: "Tier 3 Nitro Guns"
	quest.5748340466493442.quest_desc: ["A stove provides the foundation for a permanent kitchen. Keep fuel nearby and make room for ingredients and finished meals."]
	quest.5853FB39186545CA.quest_desc: ["The combustion chamber burns fuel in a monstrous More Propulsion turbojet engine. In this pack, GTCEu light fuel fills the kerosene role for these engines. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.58CA9856922BAF42.quest_desc: ["A foundry basin and ladle help you handle molten metal. Use them to transfer melt and organize a casting area beside your molds."]
	quest.59EB90336F5F41EF.quest_desc: ["Casting sand and cannon machines begin heavy ordnance production. These are industrial tools, not early weapon crafts."]
	quest.5AEBAB300FAAE99A.quest_desc: ["Wool yarn moves textiles beyond raw fiber. It leads into cloth, beds, sails, and wind power."]
	quest.5BB3B24C72823E1E.quest_desc: ["The combustion chamber burns fuel in a large More Propulsion turbojet engine. In this pack, GTCEu light fuel fills the kerosene role for these engines. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.5C1A18A9494036BD.quest_desc: ["Natural raw fireclay is commonly found in sedimentary stone around shallow coal-bearing layers. Settle it in a water barrel to convert it into refined fire clay."]
	quest.5C335E88271F6766.quest_desc: ["The compressor prepares incoming air before the combustion chamber in a large More Propulsion turbojet engine. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.5CAD3A014B4A2033.quest_desc: ["The power loom and trip hammer automate textile and heavy forging work. They reduce manual repetition without bypassing the steel stage."]
	quest.5CCA79DF998E3751.quest_desc: ["The steel mechanism is an intermediate component for TFMG equipment. Set up production of its parts to make expanding your factory easier."]
	quest.5D4A0C644A242F14.quest_desc: ["Sterling silver is an alloy branch that supports tools, components, and later material variety."]
	quest.5D914AAF6145B796.quest_desc: ["Windmills are another native mechanical power route. They depend on textile work and fit before full industrial engines."]
	quest.5D914AAF6145B796.title: "Windmill"
	quest.5DAD3DAE4D144476.quest_desc: ["The turbine sits after the combustion chamber in a small More Propulsion turbofan engine and uses energy from the hot gas flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.5DEE5207EDC15ADF.quest_desc: ["The turbine engine represents a high-output mechanical stage. Its recipe should require meaningful engine infrastructure."]
	quest.5E6A79F95A92D6C1.quest_desc: ["A paraglider turns altitude into travel distance. Choose a landing spot before taking off and keep an eye on your stamina."]
	quest.5F07DD8DC78612F2.quest_desc: ["Daub and large vessels provide early construction and ceramic utility. They are simple but remain useful for low-tech processing."]
	quest.5F1DC535A7DB60BA.quest_desc: ["The mechanical drill is a key machine component. Its recipe uses a proper drill head instead of loose iron pieces."]
	quest.5F2DB93EB21E06E6.quest_desc: ["The copper saw makes lumber production reliable. Hold the saw and right-click stripped logs or wood for support cutting where the recipe viewer shows a world interaction. Before this, stone axes can produce some planks and supports, but with worse yield and tool wear."]
	quest.5F2DB93EB21E06E6.title: "Copper Saw"
	quest.5F4993AC2F6178EA.quest_desc: ["Forge a pan bowl from a cast iron double sheet on an anvil. Add a ceramic handle to turn it into a finished skillet for cooking."]
	quest.60920470A916146F.quest_desc: ["Pre-steel javelins are early thrown weapons. They are cheaper than steel weapons, but limited by their material tier."]
	quest.60920470A916146F.title: "Pre-Steel Javelin"
	quest.6113901F3ACC904F.quest_desc: ["Wrought iron unlocks early production machines: the rolling mill, belt grinder, spring coiling machine, vacuum chamber, and millstone. Connect them to rotational power and check their available processing recipes."]
	quest.6113901F3ACC904F.title: "Wrought Iron Machines"
	quest.613C53304C480F2D.quest_desc: ["The tree tap starts natural resin collection. Conifer tapping is tied to turpentine and sticky resin processing."]
	quest.6157451FA720B7B9.quest_desc: ["Paper starts with waste wood. Boil sawdust in wood ash lye to break it down into workable fiber, then mix it with flour and dry it under gentle heat. This gives you a steady way to make writing material once wood processing is established."]
	quest.61F4EF9398DBBE1F.quest_desc: ["The combustion chamber burns fuel in a small More Propulsion turbojet engine. In this pack, GTCEu light fuel fills the kerosene role for these engines. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.63051C79408B3B8E.quest_desc: ["The power loom brings textile production onto TFC mechanical power. Supply rotation and stock up on fibers for weaving."]
	quest.630E67B9983A97F0.quest_desc: ["Rivets are small but common metal parts. They are made from stamens and rods through forging or mechanical turning routes."]
	quest.63DC4B82A6826AF7.quest_desc: ["Leather flasks and basic leather gear help with travel and survival before metal containers are common."]
	quest.656FB1E934C804DA.quest_desc: ["Compress sawdust into pellets, then pellets into briquettes. This turns sawing waste into a compact fuel supply."]
	quest.6571F69F3047163D.quest_desc: ["This bridge converts low-tech mechanical power into rotational machinery. It keeps early power grounded in physical infrastructure."]
	quest.6571F69F3047163D.title: "Mechanical Power Bridge"
	quest.65DAB1AE0E348736.quest_desc: ["Create Thrusters engines provide thrust for moving structures. The large and small versions can be converted into one another through crafting to suit your vessel."]
	quest.6664C6E21DB8B152.quest_desc: ["Steel lets you build a mechanical press, curving press, helve hammer, and mixer. These machines use rotational power to shape workpieces and prepare materials for further production."]
	quest.6664C6E21DB8B152.title: "Steel Machines"
	quest.672A3D7F2C716544.quest_desc: [
		"Cloth comes from loom work and unlocks beds, sails, windmills, clothing, and climate protection. Burlap, wool, silk, cotton, and linen each push you toward different clothing options."
		"Fabrics can also become insulation materials. Add them to clothing or armor on a Sewing Table."
		"{\"text\":\"Blue/Cyan\",\"color\":\"aqua\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" protects from cold and freezing.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"Orange\",\"color\":\"gold\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\"/\",\"color\":\"white\"},{\"text\":\"Red\",\"color\":\"red\"},{\"text\":\" protects from heat and overheating.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"Purple/Neutral\",\"color\":\"light_purple\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" protects both sides at once, but less efficiently than specialized insulation.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
		"{\"text\":\"Green/Adaptive\",\"color\":\"green\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" shifts toward the temperature problem you are currently facing.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.672A3D7F2C716544.title: "Cloth"
	quest.679ABBFCC97386E2.quest_desc: ["Graphite is required for refractory and crucible progression. Graphite dust and powder are unified through conversion recipes."]
	quest.67EC03BA2CAD3FF5.quest_desc: ["Leather is a major early material. It is used where rubber would be too advanced or too expensive for the stage."]
	quest.685D5ADFD9FDB312.quest_desc: ["Tier 5 nitro firearms require stronger materials and a more advanced chemical base than earlier nitro weapons."]
	quest.685D5ADFD9FDB312.title: "Tier 5 Nitro Guns"
	quest.687135F73A0157F8.quest_desc: ["The metal coke oven is more advanced than the early brick oven. It produces more creosote and turns one log into two charcoal, making it a better industrial charcoal route."]
	quest.68AE7C1B54E63D83.quest_desc: ["The Create millstone grinds materials using rotational power. Craft it with a cogwheel, andesite casing, and TFC handstone, then arrange input and output handling."]
	quest.69987C0B389D2624.quest_desc: ["Black steel anvils unlock the upper steel forging line and prepare red and blue steel work."]
	quest.6A12BAEEFDECF9F6.quest_desc: ["Fire clay can be made from kaolin and graphite, but natural raw fireclay is also available. Look in sedimentary regions near shallow coal, then process it in a water barrel."]
	quest.6B8AB41B4059E565.quest_desc: ["The industrial crucible handles molten materials in Create Metallurgy. Its recipe uses reinforced fire bricks; leave room nearby for material supply and casting."]
	quest.6BF6FCE80E16527E.quest_desc: ["Bronze multiblock tanks and steam casings prepare larger fluid and steam infrastructure before electricity."]
	quest.6C253000BEE7F675.quest_desc: ["The combustion chamber burns fuel in a standard More Propulsion turbofan engine. In this pack, GTCEu light fuel fills the kerosene role for these engines. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.6DB2577010ACA29C.quest_desc: ["Black steel unlocks another set of machines: the foundry mixer, lathe, and drilling equipment. Supply rotational power and make room for processing metals and components."]
	quest.6DB2577010ACA29C.title: "Black Steel Machines"
	quest.6F094FC87D3E348C.quest_desc: ["Tier 0 gunpowder firearms are the simplest steel guns. They avoid complex mechanisms and use basic black powder ammunition."]
	quest.6F094FC87D3E348C.title: "Tier 0 Gunpowder Guns"
	quest.6F24BD2659F4BCA5.quest_desc: ["The vacuum chamber handles vacuum and drying-style processing, including some rubber and resin steps where a simple mixer would be too crude."]
	quest.6F6F63274C5DDE5F.quest_desc: ["Crossbows and primitive blades are fallback ranged and melee options before industrial firearms are practical."]
	quest.7044B9A7B4470550.quest_desc: ["The compressor prepares incoming air before the combustion chamber in a large More Propulsion turbofan engine. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.717136C73DEE3C16.quest_desc: ["The nozzle forms the exhaust end of a monstrous More Propulsion turbojet engine and directs the outgoing flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.72156499578E5044.quest_desc: ["Guncotton and packed guncotton are stronger propellant stages. Packed charges are for larger or more powerful ammunition."]
	quest.7256AC92286A90A8.quest_desc: ["The turbine sits after the combustion chamber in a large More Propulsion turbofan engine and uses energy from the hot gas flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.72A8CFC5C9F55695.quest_desc: ["The steam engine is useful, but it should not replace every earlier power source. Treat it as one branch of mechanical progression."]
	quest.72C4F696BDC0122C.quest_desc: ["Sticky resin is obtained through the custom resin chain rather than early slimeballs. Use natural tree products and drying/chemical steps."]
	quest.738EEC3DDFE0A897.quest_desc: ["Bone tools give early alternatives to stone and flint. Bone parts are made by holding bones or bone scraps and right-clicking solid stone, then using the resulting parts in the tool recipes."]
	quest.7414E3054676831F.quest_desc: ["The mechanical lathe is an early analogue to a basic electrical lathe for rods, bolts, gears, and shaped parts."]
	quest.7441B37AEDB6D13F.quest_desc: ["The compressor prepares incoming air before the combustion chamber in a standard More Propulsion turbojet engine. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.745267924175CEA4.quest_desc: ["Tier 5 armor-piercing firearms use harder projectile materials and more demanding weapon construction."]
	quest.745267924175CEA4.title: "Tier 5 AP Guns"
	quest.74C4DCC5DCFEA450.quest_desc: ["Cardboard is made from coarse wood pulp. Boil sawdust in water, then bind and press the pulp with flour while applying mild heat. It is rougher than paper, but better suited for sturdy packaging and lightweight parts."]
	quest.75ABAF1E737E7593.quest_desc: ["The precision mechanism is made through sequenced assembly starting from a brass plate. Prepare the processing line and a supply of components for more advanced equipment."]
	quest.75AC90323A6D8776.quest_desc: [
		"Fur clothing is heavy cold-weather protection for winter, mountains, and polar climates. It is the wrong choice for heat, but very strong when cold exposure is the main threat."
		"{\"text\":\"Blue/Cyan\",\"color\":\"aqua\",\"extra\":[{\"text\":\" insulation reinforces what fur is already for: surviving serious cold, snow, mountains, and polar regions.\",\"color\":\"white\"}]}"
	]
	quest.75AC90323A6D8776.title: "Fur Clothes"
	quest.77C2190C3455DD29.quest_desc: ["Coal briquettes provide a compact fuel supply. Check the charcoal and honeycomb briquette recipes, as their production has been changed in this pack."]
	quest.77C2190C3455DD29.title: "Coal Briquettes"
	quest.77F5F66782875AFA.quest_desc: ["Tier 4 guncotton firearms use stronger mechanisms and materials while staying below the nitro and AP endgame."]
	quest.77F5F66782875AFA.title: "Tier 4 Guncotton Guns"
	quest.781DD8775EB68A7E.quest_desc: ["Armor-piercing bullets use hard cores such as tungsten steel. They are expensive and intended for late ammunition tiers."]
	quest.781DD8775EB68A7E.title: "AP bullets"
	quest.787DA20C2E66A0DD.quest_desc: ["The compressor prepares incoming air before the combustion chamber in a monstrous More Propulsion turbofan engine. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.792D4ADAA37091EE.quest_desc: ["Cannons require dedicated tools for drilling, building, and welding large barrels. Treat them as heavy industry."]
	quest.792D4ADAA37091EE.title: "Cannons"
	quest.79AB0164D65576FC.quest_desc: ["Bows and early thrown weapons remain useful before firearm production is stable."]
	quest.7AD30622983B5592.quest_desc: ["The basin is intentionally not a day-one block. It becomes important for heated mixing, puddling-style wrought iron automation, and later recipes."]
	quest.7B129451EB903BB5.quest_desc: ["The mechanical saw automates cutting recipes: boards, rods, bolts, and several wood and metal intermediates. This is the powered version of saw work; the hand saw still uses right-click interactions for some wood cutting."]
	quest.7B2ED766A87E8138.quest_desc: ["Tier 3 armor-piercing firearms introduce harder projectiles before the highest AP materials are available."]
	quest.7B2ED766A87E8138.title: "Tier 3 AP Guns"
	quest.7B94418FC5222F2D.quest_desc: ["The nozzle forms the exhaust end of a small More Propulsion turbofan engine and directs the outgoing flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.7B9A11689BDAAE35.quest_desc: ["The nozzle forms the exhaust end of a standard More Propulsion turbojet engine and directs the outgoing flow. Match the size and engine family of the other sections."]
	quest.7BA8E343F752FF66.quest_desc: ["Knives cover simple cutting and survival combat. Better blade materials make them more reliable."]
	quest.7BE9CB31791FC62C.quest_desc: ["Tier 0 guncotton firearms use early guncotton loads in otherwise simple steel weapons."]
	quest.7BE9CB31791FC62C.title: "Tier 0 Guncotton Guns"
	quest.7D49D9B98BE0F7F7.quest_desc: ["Lumber normally comes from saw work, but rough stone-age plank production is also possible with axes. For the rough route, use an axe with right-click: stripped logs or wood can become supports, and vertical supports can become lumber. The axe route is lossy and wears tools; the saw route is the efficient standard."]
	quest.7D49D9B98BE0F7F7.title: "Lumber"
	quest.7E5E6AE99DE606E8.quest_desc: ["Flux is required for welding and several metalworking steps. Keep a steady supply before pushing deeper into forging."]
	quest.7EAFB78EBF830BA9.quest_desc: ["Brass mechanisms and glassworking tools are precision craft foundations for later mechanical parts."]
	quest.7FAF55BA9A087E3A.quest_desc: [
		"The loom starts the real textile chain. Cloth is used for beds, wind power, sails, clothing, and climate control; linen joins burlap, wool, silk, and cotton as another useful fabric."
		"A Sewing Table lets you sew fabrics or insulation into clothing and armor. Read the insulation colors as purpose: blue/cyan for cold, orange/red for heat, purple/neutral for weaker two-way protection, and green/adaptive for changing conditions."
	]
	quest.7FAF55BA9A087E3A.title: "Loom"
	quest.7FEC1B8DC1A9F513.quest_desc: ["Advanced potato cannons are stronger utility weapons that sit above the simple handheld version."]
